# 0005. nvim-treesitter on the main branch (Neovim 0.12+)

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-11-07

## Context
The old config used the pre-rewrite API (`require("nvim-treesitter.configs")`) and pinned
nothing. When the plugin's default branch moved to the rewrite, every fresh install crashed.

## Decision
Use nvim-treesitter's `main` branch with its new API, pinned in the lockfile. Parsers are listed
once in `lua/plugins/treesitter.lua` and compiled by `make sync` (`scripts/ts-install.lua`).
On Neovim older than 0.12 treesitter is skipped with a one-time warning.

## Alternatives
- Stay on the old `master` branch: frozen upstream, would need migrating later anyway.

## Rationale
One branch for every machine keeps `lazy-lock.json` valid everywhere.

## Consequences
- Requires Neovim 0.12+ for treesitter features (Arch ships it; macOS via brew).
- The old `nvim-treesitter.configs` setup must never come back.

## References
- `lua/plugins/treesitter.lua`, commit `10539ca`
